# Build output / packaged releases
dist/

# ---- Working material that must never reach a public repository ----
# Screenshots and research PDFs sitting in the repository root. They routinely carry things that
# belong to whoever took them and to nobody else: local IP addresses, device names, the audio
# hardware in the machine, a user name in a window title. Keep them out by shape rather than by
# remembering each time.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.pdf
/*.log

# The device conversation KlangHub can write. It contains the addresses of every speaker in the
# house and what was played on them.
*.log
logs/

# Everything else that carries more than it appears to. A crash dump holds device names, addresses
# and window titles - and this project takes dumps to diagnose things, so one will sooner or later be
# sitting in the working directory when somebody types `git add .`. A capture holds the whole
# network conversation; an archive holds whatever was put in it.
*.dmp
*.mdmp
*.hdmp
*.etl
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.har
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.mp4
*.mov

# Images and PDFs anywhere, not only in the root - which is all `/*.png` ever covered. The
# application's own artwork is put back below.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.bmp
*.pdf
!Source/KlangHub/Resources/artwork.png
!Source/KlangHub/UserControls/*.png
!installer/wizard-*.bmp
!receiver/assets/*.png

# Credentials and machine-local configuration.
.env
*.pfx
*.p12
*.snk
user.config

# Recorded audio. Whatever was playing at the time is nobody else's business.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.flac
